The '''Dacia Logan''' is a family of automobiles produced and marketed jointly by the [[France|French]] manufacturer [[Renault]] and its [[Romania]]n subsidiary [[Automobile Dacia|Dacia]] since mid-2004, and was the successor to the [[Dacia 1300|Dacia 1310]] and [[Dacia Solenza]]. It has been produced as a [[Sedan (automobile)|sedan]], [[station wagon]], and as a [[pick-up truck|pick-up]]. It has been manufactured at Dacia's automobile plant in [[Mioveni]], [[Romania]], and at Renault (or its partners') plants in [[Morocco]], [[Argentina]], [[Turkey]], [[Russia]], [[Colombia]], [[Iran]] and [[India]]. The [[pickup truck|pick-up]] has also been produced at [[Nissan]]'s plant in [[Rosslyn, Gauteng|Rosslyn]], [[South Africa]].

It has also been marketed as the '''Renault Logan''', '''Nissan Aprio''', '''Mahindra Verito''', '''Renault L90''', [[Lada Largus]] (the [[#Logan I MCV|MCV]]), '''Nissan NP200''' (the [[#Logan Pick-Up|pick-up]]), [[Renault Symbol]] (Mk3), '''Renault Taliant''',  and as the '''Renault Tondar 90''' depending on the existing presence or positioning of the [[Renault]] brand.
 
Since its launch, the Dacia Logan was estimated to have reached over 4 million sales worldwide as of 2018.<ref>{{cite web |title=10 countries in 10 days in a Dacia Logan – 1/10: Romania |url=https://bestsellingcarsblog.com/2019/01/10-countries-in-10-days-in-a-dacia-logan-1-10-romania/ |publisher=Best Selling Cars Blog |access-date=10 January 2019 |date=3 January 2018}}</ref>

