</gallery>

===Features===

The Logan is based on the [[Nissan B platform|Dacia B0 platform]], also used for other [[Renault]] and [[Nissan]] models.<ref>{{cite journal|title=Dacia Lodgy. Un monospace à 10 000 €!|journal=Auto Plus|date=28 November 2011|issue=1212|pages=21|url=http://www.autonews.fr/|quote=Il ne s'agit plus de la base de la Clio 2, comme pour les autres modèles de la gamme [...]}}</ref> It has 50% fewer parts than a high-end Renault vehicle and has a limited number of [[electronics|electronic]] devices. This makes the car cheaper to produce and easier and cheaper to repair.

Some parts are also much simpler than those of its competitors. For example, rear-view mirrors are [[symmetrical]] and can be used on either side of the car, the [[windshield]] is flatter than usual, and the [[dashboard]] is a single [[injection molding|injection-molded]] piece.

The developers have taken into account several differences between road and climate conditions in developed and developing countries. The Logan suspension is soft and strong, and the chassis sits visibly higher than most other [[compact car]]s to help it negotiate dirt roads and potholes on ill-maintained asphalt roads. The engine is specially prepared to handle lower quality fuel, whereas the air conditioning is powerful enough to lower the temperature several degrees (temperatures above 40&nbsp;°C are common in the [[Middle East]] and the [[Mediterranean Sea]]).

===Trim levels===
In [[Romania]], it was initially available in four trim levels: Ambiance, Preference, Laureate and Ambition. The basic trim level, Ambiance, featured a driver airbag, optional body-coloured bumpers, wheel trims and electric door locks. The second trim level, Preference, added a passenger airbag, power steering, electric front windows, a radio, two rear seat head restraints and remote locking. The third trim level, Laureate, added front fog lights, air conditioning, a trip computer, electric mirrors, three rear seat head restraints and a multi-adjustable driver seat.<ref>{{cite web|title=Echipamente| trans-title = Equipment | url=http://www.dacia.ro/images/Echipamente.pdf|publisher=Dacia|language = ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050208005220/http://www.dacia.ro/images/Echipamente.pdf|archive-date=8 February 2005}}</ref> The top trim level, Ambition also had ABS, electric rear windows, a CD player and alloy wheels. The 1.6-litre petrol engine was only available starting with the Preference trim level.<ref>{{cite web|title=Versiuni|url=http://www.dacia.ro/logan/versiuni|publisher=Dacia|access-date=23 August 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20051205010641/http://www.dacia.ro/logan/versiuni|archive-date=5 December 2005}}</ref> In September 2005, the 1.5-litre diesel engine was introduced,<ref>{{cite web|title=Acum Logan cu motor Diesel! | trans-title = Logan now with a diesel engine! | url = http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/acum-logan-cu-motor-diesel|publisher=Dacia| language = ro|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060418084224/http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/acum-logan-cu-motor-diesel|archive-date=18 April 2006 |date=9 September 2005}}</ref> initially not being available on the Ambition trim level. In January 2006, a new intermediate trim level called Laureate Plus was added, which in addition to the Laureate trim level featured ABS, electric rear windows and a CD player. Also, the diesel engine became available for the Ambition trim level.<ref>{{cite web|title=Versiuni|url=http://www.dacia.ro/logan/versiuni|publisher=Dacia| language = ro |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060112035038/http://www.dacia.ro/logan/versiuni|archive-date=12 January 2006}}</ref>

In September 2006, several improvements were introduced to the range, such as a new button for the trunk lid, a new knob for the gear lever, crystal rear lamps, as well as new designs for the wheel trims and the alloy wheels in addition to three new paint colours.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia prezintă Noua Colecţie Logan|url=http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/dacia-prezinta-noua-colectie-logan|publisher=Dacia|access-date=23 August 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061119215346/http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/dacia-prezinta-noua-colectie-logan|archive-date=19 November 2006 |date=14 September 2006}}</ref> Also, the new top of the range level Prestige was introduced, which featured larger door mirrors, body-coloured bumpers (entirely), side moldings and door handles, leather-trimmed gear lever and steering wheel, as well as other interior refinements. It was only available with a new 1.6-litre 16-valve petrol engine, which developed {{cvt|105|hp-metric|kW|0}}.<ref>{{cite web|title=Versiuni|url=http://www.dacia.ro/logan/versiuni|publisher=Dacia|access-date=23 August 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061006074328/http://www.dacia.ro/logan/versiuni|archive-date=6 October 2006}}</ref>

In July 2007, a more powerful version of the 1.5-litre diesel engine was added, developing {{cvt|85|hp-metric|kW|0}}. It was initially made available only for the [[station wagon]], on the Preference and Laureate levels,<ref>{{cite web|title=Un nou motor diesel pe Dacia Logan MCV|url=http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/un-nou-motor-diesel-pe-dacia-logan-mcv|publisher=Dacia|access-date=23 August 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070706203851/http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/un-nou-motor-diesel-pe-dacia-logan-mcv|archive-date=6 July 2007|date=3 July 2007}}</ref> and in September 2007, it also became available for the sedan version, on the Laureate, Ambition and Prestige levels.<ref>{{cite web|title=Un nou motor diesel 1.5 dCi, de 85 CP|url=http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/Un%20nou%20motor%20diesel%201.5%20dCi,%20de%2085%20CP|publisher=Dacia|access-date=23 August 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071117221853/http://www.dacia.ro/noutati/Un%20nou%20motor%20diesel%201.5%20dCi%2C%20de%2085%20CP|archive-date=17 November 2007|date=3 September 2007|url-status=dead|df=dmy-all}}</ref>

In June 2009, the new 1.2-litre 16-valve petrol engine was added for both the Logan and the Sandero. The engine was capable of developing a maximum power of {{cvt|75|hp-metric|kW|0}} and {{convert|107|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque.<ref>{{cite web|title=Noul motor 1.2 16 V 75 CP, disponibil pe modelele Dacia Logan berlina si Sandero|url=http://www.daciagroup.com/presa/comunicate-de-presa/2009/noul-motor-12-16-v-75-cp-disponibil-pe-modelele-dacia-logan-berlina|publisher=Dacia|access-date=4 January 2014|date=22 June 2009}}</ref>

===Safety===
In June 2005, the car achieved a three-star rating at the [[Euro NCAP]] crash tests.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.euroncap.com/tests/dacia_logan_2005/221.aspx |title=Dacia Logan |publisher=Euro NCAP |access-date=9 October 2010}}</ref> This result confirms initial expectations stated previously by Renault.

Depending on the equipment level, standard on some variants and optional on others, the facelifted Logan comes with driver, passenger and side airbags.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia New Logan brochure|url=http://www.daciamodellen.nl/docs/ro-brochure-dacia-logan-sedan-2008-08.pdf|publisher=Dacia|access-date=9 September 2013|date=28 August 2008|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304054041/http://www.daciamodellen.nl/docs/ro-brochure-dacia-logan-sedan-2008-08.pdf|archive-date=4 March 2016|url-status=dead}}</ref> In terms of active safety, all versions feature the latest generation Bosch 8.1 ABS, which incorporates EBD (electronic brakeforce distribution) and EBA (emergency brake assist).

===Engines===
When the Logan appeared, all engines complied to the Euro 3 standard and since January 2007, all engines have complied with the Euro 4 standard, including the diesel engine, whose power has increased to 70&nbsp;hp.

