===Marketing and production===
[[File:Renault Logan.JPG|thumb|right|Renault Logan assembled by Avtoframos (Russia)]]
The Logan, vital to increasing sales of the Renault group to the 4 million mark by 2010, is manufactured in nine production and operational assembly centres: Romania (Automobile Dacia), the pilot plant of the Logan Programme, Russia ([[Avtoframos]]), Morocco ([[Somaca]]), Colombia ([[Sofasa]]), Iran (two assembly plants ([[Iran Khodro]] and [[Pars Khodro]]) supervised by [[Renault Pars|Renault-Pars]]), India ([[Mahindra & Mahindra Limited|Mahindra]]), Brazil (Renault),<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.renault.com/en/Lists/ArchivesDocuments/Renault%20-%202007%20Registration%20Document.pdf |page=45 |title=2007 Registration Document |publisher=Renault |date=17 April 2008 |access-date=19 June 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110815223211/http://www.renault.com/en/Lists/ArchivesDocuments/Renault%20-%202007%20Registration%20Document.pdf |archive-date=15 August 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref> and South Africa ([[Nissan South Africa]]).<ref name="renault">{{cite web|title=2011 Registration Document|url=http://www.renault.com/en/lists/archivesdocuments/renault%20-%202011%20registration%20document.pdf|publisher=Renault|page=21|date=23 March 2012|access-date=5 September 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121207171628/http://www.renault.com/en/Lists/ArchivesDocuments/Renault%20-%202011%20Registration%20Document.pdf|archive-date=7 December 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> The [[Complete knock down|CKD]] centre is named the International Logistics Network and is located near the [[Mioveni]] plant in [[Romania]]. It is the biggest logistic centre of its kind, not only within the Renault Group but in the entire global automotive industry.<ref name="Project"/>

====Dacia models====
In markets where Renault has a presence, such as Europe (Russia, Belarus and Ukraine excepted), Turkey, the Maghreb, and Chile, it is generally sold as the Dacia Logan.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.daciagroup.com/eKontentDaciaXFiles/home_ro/ventes/rseau_monde/dacia_pe_glob/index.html |title=Distribution of Dacia throughout the world |publisher=Dacia Group |access-date=9 October 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110708220248/http://daciagroup.com/eKontentDaciaXFiles/home_ro/ventes/rseau_monde/dacia_pe_glob/index.html |archive-date=8 July 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

====Renault & Nissan models====
Exceptions are South Africa, Argentina, Russia, Ukraine,{{#tag:ref|In Ukraine, it was marketed under the Dacia marque until September 2009.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia |url=http://www.dacia.ua/ |publisher=Dacia Ukraine |date=17 September 2009 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100211140227/http://www.dacia.ua/ |archive-date=11 February 2010 }}</ref>|group=nb}} Colombia, Ecuador, Israel, Egypt, Brazil, Chile, Peru, Saudi Arabia, India, Nepal and Venezuela where it is marketed as the ''Renault Logan'', and furthermore Mexico, where the Logan was sold as the ''Nissan Aprio'', given the better reputation of the Japanese brand and stronger brand recognition of Nissan itself in the Mexican market.<ref group="nb" name="nissan"/> The Nissan Aprio has the 1.6-litre 16 valve [[straight-four engine]] with a 5-speed [[Manual transmission|manual]] or 4-speed [[automatic transmission]],<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.post-gazette.com/pg/06277/727315-185.stm/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061024130425/http://www.post-gazette.com/pg/06277/727315-185.stm |url-status=dead |archive-date=24 October 2006 |title=Inexpensive Logan boosts Renault in emerging markets |publisher=Post-gazette.com |date=4 October 2006 |access-date=9 October 2010 | first1=Norihiko | last1=Shirouzu | first2=Stephen | last2=Power}}</ref> and was assembled in Brazil.<ref>{{cite web|title=Atlas Renault – Édition Septembre 2008|url=http://www.renault.com/fr/Lists/ArchivesDocuments/Renault%20-%20Atlas%20-%20fr%20-sept08.pdf|page=9;31|publisher=Renault|date=28 September 2008|access-date=27 January 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120106013844/http://www.renault.com/fr/Lists/ArchivesDocuments/Renault%20-%20Atlas%20-%20fr%20-sept08.pdf|archive-date=6 January 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> It was later discontinued from that market in August 2010, due to decreasing sales, and the [[Nissan Tiida|Versa]] replaced it for the 2012 model year.<ref>{{cite news|title=Descontinúan Nissan Aprio en México desde agosto|url=http://www.alvolante.info/nacionales/descontinuan-nissan-aprio-en-mexico-desde-agosto/|newspaper=Alvolante.info|access-date=5 September 2012|date=14 September 2010}}</ref>

In Brazil, it was manufactured by Renault at the [[São José dos Pinhais]] factory since 2007, with the facelifted model being introduced in 2010.<ref>{{cite web|title=Novo Renault Logan parte de R$ 28.690|url=http://g1.globo.com/Noticias/Carros/0,,MUL1567877-9658,00.html|publisher=Globo.com|access-date=6 September 2012|date=13 April 2010}}</ref>

In [[South Africa]], only the pick-up version was manufactured, at the Nissan factory in Rosslyn,{{#tag:ref|[[Nissan]] is the partner of [[Renault]] in the [[Renault–Nissan Alliance]].|group=nb|name=nissan}} starting from 2009.<ref name="renault"/><gallery widths="200" heights="140">
