====India====
In India, the Logan was marketed as the ''Mahindra Renault Logan''.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.mahindrarenault.com/ |title=Mahindra Logan |publisher=Mahindra Renault |access-date=9 October 2010}}</ref> In 2005, Renault partnered the Indian utility and commercial vehicles manufacturer [[Mahindra & Mahindra]] (M&M). The Logan was launched in [[India]] in April 2007, as a collaboration with Mahindra, who helped Renault cut costs by 15%.<ref>{{cite book|last1=Sirkin|first1=Harold L.|url=https://archive.org/details/globalitycompeti00sirk/page/304|title=GLOBALITY: Competing with Everyone from Everywhere for Everything'|last2=Hemerling|first2=James W.|last3=Bhattacharya|first3=Arindam K.|date=11 June 2008|publisher=Business Plus|isbn=978-0-446-17829-7|location=New York|page=[https://archive.org/details/globalitycompeti00sirk/page/304 304]|url-access=registration|df=dmy-all}}</ref> India was the first [[Left- and right-hand traffic|right-hand drive]] market for the Logan. Logan could not make it in the Indian market, selling just over 44,000 vehicles since then, with an additional 2,600 vehicles in Nepal and South Africa where M&M also held the licence to sell the Logan.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.hindustantimes.com/rssfeed/auto/Mahindra-buys-out-Renault-in-Logan-venture/Article1-532209.aspx |title=Mahindra buys out Renault in Logan venture |work=Hindustan Times |date=16 April 2010 | url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110605233505/http://www.hindustantimes.com/rssfeed/auto/Mahindra-buys-out-Renault-in-Logan-venture/Article1-532209.aspx |archive-date=5 June 2011 |df=dmy-all }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.financialexpress.com/news/renault-exits-mahindra-jv/607367/ |title=Renault exits from Logan JV, M&M gets licence |work=The Financial Express |date=16 April 2010 |access-date=9 October 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100420161903/http://www.financialexpress.com/news/renault-exits-mahindra-jv/607367 |archive-date=20 April 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref> In April 2010, it was announced that the M&M had bought out Renault's 49% in the Mahindra-Renault joint venture. The new agreement gave M&M more flexibility in engineering the car to suit the needs of the Indian consumer. The Logan was marketed with the Mahindra-Renault logo until the end of March 2011.

=====Mahindra Verito=====
[[File:Mahindra Verito Vibe 2015.JPG|left|thumb|The [[Mahindra Verito Vibe]] notchback derived from the Logan model]]
Following the dissolution of the Indian joint venture between [[Renault India Private Limited|Renault India]] and M&M in 2010, Mahindra retained the rights to produce and sell the Logan under its own name of ''Mahindra Verito'', with minor alterations to the front, but retaining Renault diesel engines.<ref>{{cite web|title=Logan now renamed into Verito|url=http://indiaautoindustry.blogspot.com/2011/04/logan-now-renamed-into-verito.html|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120709191731/http://indiaautoindustry.blogspot.com/2011/04/logan-now-renamed-into-verito.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=9 July 2012|publisher=India Auto Industry|access-date=13 January 2012|date=25 April 2011}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|date=27 April 2011|title=Mahindra launches Verito sedan: drops Renault badges, name|url=http://www.carmayogi.in/new-a-event/197-mahinda-verito.html|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110911192643/http://www.carmayogi.in/new-a-event/197-mahinda-verito.html|archive-date=11 September 2011|access-date=27 April 2011|publisher=Carmayogi.in}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Why Choose Verito|url=http://www.mahindraverito.com/why_choose_verito.html|publisher=Mahindra Verito|access-date=26 January 2012|archive-date=3 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303232214/http://www.mahindraverito.com/why_choose_verito.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> On 26 July 2012, a facelifted version of the car was revealed by Mahindra in [[New Delhi]],<ref>{{cite web|title=2012 Mahindra Verito Facelift launched at Rs 5.27 lakh|url=http://www.oncars.in/Car-News-Detail/2012-Mahindra-Verito-Facelift-launched-at-Rs-5-27-lakh/2775|publisher=OnCars.in|date=26 July 2012|access-date=5 September 2012|archive-date=29 July 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120729044645/http://www.oncars.in/Car-News-Detail/2012-Mahindra-Verito-Facelift-launched-at-Rs-5-27-lakh/2775|url-status=dead}}</ref> and on 5 June 2013, a [[notchback]] version was launched in [[Mumbai]], called the [[Mahindra Verito Vibe]].<ref>{{cite web|title=2013 Mahindra Verito Vibe Launched At Rs 5.63 Lakh Ex-Mumbai|url=http://overdrive.in/news/2013-mahindra-verito-vibe-launched-at-rs-5-63-lakh-ex-mumbai/|publisher=Overdrive|access-date=5 August 2013|date=5 June 2013}}</ref> Production was shut down on 31 December 2019.

An electric version of the Verito sedan and its notchback version Verito Vibe was sold as the ''Mahindra eVerito'' from 2016.<ref>{{cite web|title=eVerito|url=http://www.mahindraelectric.com/everito/|publisher=Mahindra Electric|access-date=29 April 2018}}</ref> Production was shut down on 31 December 2019.

====Iran====
[[File:Saipa-Renault Pars Tondar 2024-05-04.jpg|thumb|Renault Pars Tondar]]
In 2007, the Logan branded as ''Renault Tondar 90'' (also called Renault L90), began to be marketed in Iran by [[Renault Pars|Renault-Pars]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.renault.co.ir/cars/Logan/home.html|title=Renault Tondar|access-date=26 January 2012|publisher=Renault Pars|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120104093156/http://renault.co.ir/cars/Logan/home.html|archive-date=4 January 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> manufactured by [[Pars Khodro]] and [[Iran Khodro]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.payvand.com/news/06/jun/1231.html |title=First Logan manufactured in Iran |publisher=Payvand.com |access-date=28 April 2009 |archive-date=23 March 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200323081447/http://www.payvand.com/news/06/jun/1231.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> In the first month of production more than 100,000 Tondar 90 had been ordered.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.informatiiauto.ro/renault-logan-comandat-de-100000-iranieni-sid1001.html |title=Renault Logan comandat de 100.000 iranieni |publisher=Informaţii Auto |access-date=27 November 2010 |archive-date=25 June 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180625050158/http://www.informatiiauto.ro/renault-logan-comandat-de-100000-iranieni-sid1001.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> Renault Pars is a joint venture, 51 percent of which belongs to Renault of France. Forty-nine percent of Renault Pars' shares is jointly held by [[Industrial Development and Renovation Organization of Iran|Iran's Industrial Development and Renovation Organization]], [[IKCO]] and [[Saipa Group]]. The company was established in 2003.{{citation needed|date=July 2021}} In 2010, IKCO and Pars Khodro started to produce CNG Tondar 90s which can run on both petrol and CNG. They stopped producing CNG models in 2012. In 2013, IKCO started to produce Tondar 90s with automatic gearbox and they also made it comply with the Euro IV standards. A facelifted version is sold as the Tondar 90+, along with the original one.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://renault-iran.com/en/cars/tondar-90-plus/index.html|title=Renault TONDAR 90+ &#124; Renault Iran|website=renault-iran.com}}</ref> There is also a pickup version called the Tondar Pick-Up.<ref>{{cite web |title=Renault TONDAR PICK-UP |url= http://renault.co.ir/en/cars/tondar-pickup/index.html |publisher= Renault Iran |access-date= 28 April 2018}}</ref> In 2014 Renault updated the transmission of Logan for Iranian market using JHQ gearbox instead of regular JH3 to make the car more reliable.

By 2018, Renault had left the Iranian market but in 2023, Pars Khodro released a [[Facelift (automotive)|facelifted]] version of the original Dacia Logan called ''Pars Khodro Cadilla'' with over 85 percent local parts content.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.carscoops.com/2020/11/iranian-carmaker-to-restart-old-dacia-logan-production-without-renaults-involvement/|title=Iranian Carmaker To Restart Old Dacia Logan Production Without Renault's Involvement| first = Dan | last = Mihalascu | date=November 14, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-01-18 |title=عکس {{!}} نسخه ایرانی ال ۹۰ با نام کادیلا روانه بازار می‌شود |url=https://www.khabaronline.ir/news/1720742/عکس-نسخه-ایرانی-ال-۹۰-با-نام-کادیلا-روانه-بازار-می-شود |access-date=2023-01-25 |website=خبرآنلاین |language=fa}}</ref> The Cadila uses the 1.6-litre Saipa ME16 engine, which is actually an updated version of the [[PSA TU engine|PSA TU5]] engine.<ref>{{Cite web |title=سهند و کادیلا توسط پارس‌خودرو تولید خواهند شد | url=https://www.pedal.ir/pars-khodro/pars-khodro-sahand-cadila/ | trans-title = Sahand and Cadila will be produced by Pars Khodro | work = Pedal Magazine | access-date=2023-01-25 |date = 2023-01-19 | language=fa-IR}}</ref>

====Electric versions====
=====United States=====
In the United States, an attempt at marketing electric versions of the wagon, the van and the pick-up as the ''EMC E36'' was launched by the EnVision Motor Company, based in [[Des Moines, Iowa|Des Moines]], Iowa.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia Logan Electric Pickup for the U.S.|url=http://www.autoevolution.com/news/dacia-logan-electric-pickup-for-the-us-16426.html|publisher=Autoevolution|date=7 February 2010}}</ref> The automobiles were assembled by Dacia in Romania<ref>{{Cite web|url = https://www.greenoptimistic.com/emc-electric-vehicle-dacia-logan-20100207/|title = EMC Launches Affordable Electric Vehicle Based on Dacia Logan|date = 7 February 2010|access-date = 16 November 2020|archive-date = 13 February 2021|archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210213150413/https://www.greenoptimistic.com/emc-electric-vehicle-dacia-logan-20100207/|url-status = dead}}</ref> and powered by an [[asynchronous motor]] with a range of {{cvt|200|mi}} per charge, giving a top highway speed as high as {{cvt|75|mph}}. EMC planned to use regenerative braking and is coupled to an automatic shiftless button transmission. The battery can be charged through a [[SAE J1772|J1772]] plug or from wall outlets of either 120 or 240 volts.  This venture has since collapsed into bankruptcy.<ref>{{cite web|title=EMC Brochure|url=http://www.electricmobilecars.com/Electric_Mobile_Cars/Home_files/EMC%20Brochure.pdf|publisher=Electric Mobile Cars|date=10 October 2011|access-date=26 November 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160309124853/http://electricmobilecars.com/electric_mobile_cars/home_files/emc%20brochure.pdf|archive-date=9 March 2016|url-status=dead}}</ref>

=====Russia=====
The Lada e-Largus was announced on August 8, 2022,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.carscoops.com/2022/08/lada-e-largus-based-on-previous-gen-dacia-logan-could-become-avtovazs-first-ev/|title=Lada e-Largus Based On Previous-Gen Dacia Logan Could Become AvtoVAZ's First EV|date=8 August 2022 }}</ref> being a fully electric version based on the Largus Furgon model, and AvtoVAZ's first production electric vehicle since the Ellada in the early 2010s.

====Production====
Logan production began with a 4-door [[sedan (car)|sedan]], followed by a [[station wagon|wagon]] in September 2006. Four other models, a [[pick-up truck]], a [[panel van]], a related [[hatchback]] (the [[Dacia Sandero|Sandero]]) and a facelifted sedan followed in 2007 and 2008. Dacia sales for 2006 were over €1.5 billion, 19.6% more than in 2005. Annual production has reached almost 250,000 cars, half for exports. As of March 2009, more than 1.3 million vehicles on the Logan platform have been sold worldwide.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/do/News/articleId=143467#2 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090311223811/http://www.edmunds.com/insideline/do/News/articleId%3D143467#2 |title=Renault Launches Sandero in South Africa |publisher=Edmunds.com |date=9 March 2009 |archive-date=11 March 2009 |access-date=9 October 2010 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}</ref> On 3 September 2009, it was announced that one million Dacia cars on the Logan platform X90 have been produced at the Mioveni plant: 576,887 Logans, 246,869 Logan MCVs, 144,931 Sanderos and Stepways, 19,897 Logan VANs and 11,416 Logan Pick-Ups.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.romaniantimes.at/news/Business/2009-09-03/2704/_One_million_Dacia_cars_produced_at_Mioveni_plant__ |title=One million Dacia cars produced at Mioveni plant |work=Romanian Times |access-date=9 October 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110706094225/http://www.romaniantimes.at/news/Business/2009-09-03/2704/_One_million_Dacia_cars_produced_at_Mioveni_plant__ |archive-date=6 July 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

One of the reasons for the increase in sales is the dependability of Dacia cars. In a recent survey conducted by a French magazine, Dacia cars were voted one of the safest cars in France. Another reason is their low maintenance and repair costs. According to the survey, Dacia cars were the cheapest to maintain and repair.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.dacialogan.org/dacia-wins-kudos/ |title=Dacia wins Kudos |publisher=Dacia Logan |date=13 January 2010 |access-date=9 October 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101126140101/http://www.dacialogan.org/dacia-wins-kudos/ |archive-date=26 November 2010 |url-status=dead }}</ref> In Germany, Dacia was placed on the second position in the 2010 Vehicle Ownership Satisfaction Study released by [[J. D. Power and Associates]] in June 2010.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.autoevolution.com/news/dacia-and-bmw-go-head-to-head-in-satisfaction-study-21735.html |title=Dacia and BMW Go Head to Head in Satisfaction Study |date=24 June 2010 |publisher=Autoevolution.com |access-date=9 October 2010}}</ref>

===<span class="anchor" id="Logan I MCV"></span><span class="anchor" id="first generation MCV"></span>Logan MCV===
The Logan MCV (''Multi Convivial Vehicle''), launched at the [[2006 Paris Motor Show]], is the [[station wagon]] version of the Logan.<ref name="Logan MCV">{{cite web|title=Logan MCV: space, versatility and value for money|url=http://www.daciagroup.com/en/press/press-releases/2006/logan-mcv-space-versatility-and-value-for-money|publisher=Dacia|date=26 September 2006}}</ref> It has 5- or 7-seat versions, with a luggage space between 200 and 2,350 litres depending on how many seats are folded, and numerous storage spaces for smaller objects. It has a wheelbase longer by {{convert|275|mm|in|1|abbr=on}} than the [[sedan (car)|saloon]], and larger rear doors for easy access to the third row of seats.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia Logan MCV car volumes|url=http://www.renault-dacia-logan.com/dacia-logan-mcv-volumes.php|publisher=Renault-Dacia-Logan.com|access-date=27 November 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130601083432/http://www.renault-dacia-logan.com/dacia-logan-mcv-volumes.php|archive-date=1 June 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> It uses the same engines as the [[sedan (car)|saloon]],<ref name="Logan MCV" /> and an important improvement was the availability of side [[airbag]]s.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia Logan MCV car safety|url=http://www.renault-dacia-logan.com/dacia-logan-mcv-safety.php|publisher=Renault-Dacia-Logan.com|access-date=27 November 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130601062734/http://www.renault-dacia-logan.com/dacia-logan-mcv-safety.php|archive-date=1 June 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> It has been considered a competitor for [[compact MPV]]s, for its dimensions and the 7-seat capacity.<ref>{{cite web|title=Évaluation détaillée de la DACIA Logan MCV 7 places|url=http://www.latribuneauto.com/impression-evaluation-DACI-LOGM-BK-07-1397-dacia-logan-mcv-7-places.html|publisher=La Tribune Auto|access-date=27 November 2012|archive-date=12 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160312151644/http://latribuneauto.com/impression-evaluation-daci-logm-bk-07-1397-dacia-logan-mcv-7-places.html|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Sales on the Romanian market began in October 2006 with prices ranging between €8,200 and €12,550,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://masini.acasa.ro/noutati/logan-mcv-spatiu-si-polivalenta-la-cel-mai-bun-pret-24642.html |title=Logan MCV : spatiu si polivalenta la cel mai bun pret |publisher=Acasa.ro |access-date=27 November 2010 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110820181718/http://masini.acasa.ro/noutati/logan-mcv-spatiu-si-polivalenta-la-cel-mai-bun-pret-24642.html |archive-date=20 August 2011 |url-status=dead }}</ref> while sales to other countries began in early 2007. A revised version, with the new lights and bumper from the New Logan [[sedan (car)|saloon]], was released in late 2008. As of June 2010, Dacia produced 300,000 Logan MCVs.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.autoevolution.com/news/dacia-rolls-out-300000th-logan-mcv-21877.html |title=Dacia Rolls Out 300,000th Logan MCV |date=29 June 2010 |publisher=Autoevolution.com |access-date=9 October 2010}}</ref>

Since 2012 it is also produced in [[Russia]] by [[AvtoVAZ]] as [[Lada Largus]].<ref name="autovesti">{{cite web|title="АвтоВАЗ" выпустил вторую партию универсала Largus|url=http://auto.vesti.ru/doc.html?id=436213|publisher=Auto.Vesti.ru|date=24 January 2012|access-date=9 February 2012}}</ref> This version was first exhibited at the 2010 Moscow International Motor Show as the [[Lada]] Project R90.<ref>{{cite web |title=Moscú 2010: Lada R90 Project |url=http://es.autoblog.com/2010/08/25/moscu-2010-lada-r90-project/ |publisher=[[Autoblog.com|Autoblog]] Español |date=25 August 2010 |access-date=27 November 2010 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100901063331/http://es.autoblog.com/2010/08/25/moscu-2010-lada-r90-project/ |archive-date=1 September 2010 |df=dmy-all }}</ref> It is also offered with crossover-style body elements as the Largus Cross.<ref>{{cite web |title=LADA Official Website |url=https://www.lada.ru/en/ |website=LADA |access-date=14 August 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210802222700/https://www.lada.ru/en/ |archive-date=2 August 2021 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

