===<span class="anchor" id="Van"></span><span class="anchor" id="first generation MCV"></span>Logan Van===
[[File:Dacia Logan Van rear - PSM 2009.jpg|left|thumb|Dacia Logan Van]]
The [[panel van]] variant of the Logan was launched on 23 January 2007 in Bucharest.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia sets out to conquer the commercial vehicle market with Logan VAN|url=http://www.daciagroup.com/en/press-releases/dacia-sets-out-to-conquer-the-commercial-vehicle-market-with-logan-van.html|publisher=Dacia Group|date=23 January 2007|access-date=26 January 2012}}{{Dead link|date=July 2019 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> It is a small business oriented vehicle, with 2,500 litre loading space and 800&nbsp;kg payload. The Logan Van is more or less an MCV without the rear side windows and therefore has the same safety features and uses the same engines as the other models (except the 1.6 16v engine). Production of this model was stopped in August 2012. Since its launch, over 53,000 units were manufactured.<ref>{{cite web |date=20 September 2012 |title=Productia de utilitare Dacia, mutata definitiv in Maroc |url=http://transporter.ro/s-10255-Stiri-Productia-de-utilitare-Dacia--mutata-definitiv-in-Maroc |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160305020144/http://transporter.ro/s-10255-stiri-productia-de-utilitare-dacia--mutata-definitiv-in-maroc |archive-date=5 March 2016 |access-date=29 September 2012 |publisher=Transporter.ro}}</ref> The panel van version continues to be produced as the [[Lada Largus]] by AvtoVAZ.{{clear}}

===<span class="anchor" id="Pickup"></span><span class="anchor" id="Pick-up"></span><span class="anchor" id="Nissan NP200"></span>Logan Pick-Up===
The [[coupé utility]] version of the Logan, also based on the MCV, was introduced on 10 September 2007 (4 October 2007 at the Bucharest International Motor Show),<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.automarket.ro/stiri/premiera-mondiala-logan-pick-up-s-a-lansat-la-siab-6723.html |title=Premiera mondiala: Logan Pick-up s-a lansat la SIAB |publisher=AutoMarket.ro |access-date=27 November 2010}}</ref> as a replacement for the [[Dacia Pick-Up]]. Sales began in Romania in 2008, with the price ranging between €7,300 and €9,450.

The Logan Pick-Up was discontinued by Dacia in July 2012,<ref>{{cite web |title=Productia de Logan Pick-up, MCV si Van inceteaza anul acesta in Romania |url=http://www.4tuning.ro/vanzari-economie/productia-de-logan-pick-up-mcv-si-van-inceteaza-14939.html |access-date=24 July 2012 |publisher=4tuning.ro}}</ref> and it was not until October 2020 that the company introduced a new  [[Dacia Duster#Duster Pick-Up|pickup model based on the Dacia Duster]].<ref name="Bakkie">{{cite web |date=2020-10-23 |title=New Renault Duster 4x4 Bakkie Launched |url=https://www.cars.co.za/motoring_news/new-renault-duster-4x4-bakkie-launched/50105/ |access-date=2020-10-29 |publisher=cars.co.za}}</ref>

Starting October 2008, the Logan Pick-Up is sold in South Africa as the '''Nissan NP200'''. Visually similar to the original model at launch,<ref>{{cite web|title=Nissan starts LCV global product offensive with NP200|url=http://www.nissan-global.com/EN/NEWS/2008/_STORY/080929-04-e.html|publisher=Nissan|access-date=6 September 2012|date=29 September 2008|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120109061015/http://www.nissan-global.com/EN/NEWS/2008/_STORY/080929-04-e.html|archive-date=9 January 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> it received a light facelift in early 2009.<ref>{{cite web|title=Nissan NP200 gets a make over|url=http://www.focusontransport.co.za/regulars/market-review/64-nissan-np200-gets-a-make-over.html|publisher=Focus on Transport & Logistics|access-date=6 September 2012|date=4 June 2009|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120626064847/http://www.focusontransport.co.za/regulars/market-review/64-nissan-np200-gets-a-make-over.html|archive-date=26 June 2012|url-status=dead}}</ref> It is being built at the Nissan plant outside Pretoria, alongside the [[Renault Sandero]], and is also exported to several Southern Africa countries such as Zimbabwe, Mozambique, Namibia, Zambia, Kenya, Uganda, Seychelles and Botswana.<ref>{{cite web|access-date=2023-04-04|title=NP200 {{!}} Across Zimbabwe {{!}} Nissan Clover Leaf Motors|url=https://www.cloverleaf.co.zw/nissan/new-cars/np200/|website=www.cloverleaf.co.zw|archive-date=4 April 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230404220606/https://www.cloverleaf.co.zw/nissan/new-cars/np200/|url-status=dead}}<!-- auto-translated by Module:CS1 translator --></ref><ref>{{cite web|access-date=2023-04-04|title=NP200 {{!}} Namibia {{!}} Pupkewitz Nissan|url=https://www.pupkewitz-motors.com/nissan/new-cars/np200/|website=www.pupkewitz-motors.com}}<!-- auto-translated by Module:CS1 translator --></ref><ref>{{cite web|access-date=2023-04-04|language=en-ZA|title=Demo NISSAN NP200 1.6 For Sale {{!}} NTT Motor Group|url=https://www.nttnissan.co.bw/used_car/nissan-np200-1-6-p-u-s-c/|website=NTT Nissan Botswana|archive-date=4 April 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230404220606/https://www.nttnissan.co.bw/used_car/nissan-np200-1-6-p-u-s-c/|url-status=dead}}<!-- auto-translated by Module:CS1 translator --></ref><ref>{{cite web|access-date=2023-04-04|title=Nissan|url=https://www.nissanzambia.co.zm/new-vehicles/browse-range/np200/|website=www.nissanzambia.co.zm}}<!-- auto-translated by Module:CS1 translator --></ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Nissan |url=https://www.nissankenya.com/new-vehicles/browse-range/np200/ |access-date=2023-04-05 |website=www.nissankenya.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Nissan |url=https://www.nissan.co.ug/new-vehicles/browse-range/np200/ |access-date=2023-04-05 |website=www.nissan.co.ug}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Nissan |url=https://www.nissanseychelles.com/new-vehicles/browse-range/np200/ |access-date=2023-04-05 |website=www.nissanseychelles.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Nissan |url=https://www.nissan.co.mz/en/new-vehicles/browse-range/np200/ |access-date=2023-04-04 |website=www.nissan.co.mz |archive-date=4 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230404220606/https://www.nissan.co.mz/en/new-vehicles/browse-range/np200/ |url-status=dead }}<!-- auto-translated by Module:CS1 translator --></ref> In March 2024, the NP200 was discontinued.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Classen |first=Robin |title=The end of the half-tonner in SA: Nissan finally discontinues NP200 bakkie |url=https://www.news24.com/life/motoring/bakkies-suvs/the-end-of-the-half-tonner-in-sa-nissan-finally-discontinues-np200-bakkie-20230808 |access-date=2024-04-11 |magazine=Life |language=en-US}}</ref>

As of 2016, it is also offered in Iran as the Renault Tondar Pick-Up.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://renault-iran.com/en/cars/tondar-pickup/index.html|title=Renault Tondar Pick-Up &#124; Renault Iran|website=renault-iran.com}}</ref>

