The second generation Logan was revealed by Dacia at the [[2012 Paris Motor Show]]. Official photos with the new Logan were released on 17 September 2012.<ref name="automobile">{{cite web|title=Dacia Logan 2 – Madame Plus|url=http://www.automobile-magazine.fr/actualites/dacia/dacia_logan_2|publisher=L'Automobile Magazine|date=17 September 2012|access-date=17 September 2012|archive-date=8 April 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160408125113/http://www.automobile-magazine.fr/actualites/dacia/dacia_logan_2|url-status=dead}}</ref> It shares the same front end design with the second generation [[Dacia Sandero|Sandero]], also revealed at the motor show, as well as other elements too.<ref name="paris">{{cite web|title=Noile Dacia Logan, Sandero şi Sandero Stepway|url=http://www.daciagroup.com/presa/comunicate-de-presa/2012/noile-dacia-logan-sandero-si-sandero-stepway|publisher=Dacia|date=27 September 2012}}</ref>

According to Dacia, 60% of the design work was carried out in Romania, at Renault's engineering centre.<ref name="erde_tungaa">{{cite web |title=Cum arătau schiţele cu noile modele Dacia Logan, Sandero şi Sandero Stepway acum 3 ani |url=https://www.economica.net/cum-aratau-schitele-cu-noile-modele-dacia-logan-sandero-si-sandero-stepway-galerie-foto_40777.html |publisher=Economica.net |access-date=6 July 2019 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20190706154926/https://www.economica.net/cum-aratau-schitele-cu-noile-modele-dacia-logan-sandero-si-sandero-stepway-galerie-foto_40777.html |url-status=live |archive-date=6 July 2019 |language=ro |date=13 December 2012 }}</ref>

===Features===
Among the new features introduced with the new model there was a new three-cylinder turbocharged 0.9-litre petrol engine and capable of developing {{convert|90|hp|kW|0|abbr=on}} and {{convert|135|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}}. The other two engine options are the 1.2-litre 16-valve petrol engine, initially available also as an [[Autogas|LPG]] variant, and the 1.5-litre diesel engine, available with two power outputs.<ref name="paris"/> Their performance figures are predominantly similar to the ones of the second generation [[Dacia Sandero#Engines 2|Sandero]].<ref name="versiuni"/> Later, the 1.2-litre [[Autogas|LPG]] variant was discontinued, in favor of the 0.9 TCe, as the first did not meet the new Euro 6 emission standards.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.autolatest.ro/editorial-auto/dacia-nu-renunt-la-gpl-noul-motor-pe-gaz-este-0-9-tce-si-corespunde-normelor-euro-6|title=Dacia nu renunta la GPL! Noul motor pe gaz este 0.9 TCE si corespunde normelor Euro 6|date=8 May 2015}}</ref>

Another addition was the Media Nav system, already introduced earlier in the same year on the [[Dacia Lodgy|Lodgy]], consisting of a 7-inch touchscreen display with multimedia functions and a navigation software included. Other new features are [[speed limiter]], cruise control, rear parking sensors, and front and side airbags, as well as ABS and ESP, as standard.<ref name="paris"/> The interior has been significantly revised, with new chromed elements added, and the hood is now supported with a [[strut]]. A new Eco button, placed on the dashboard, limits the engine revs to 4,000 rpm.<ref name="0-100">{{cite web|title=Noile Sandero si Logan in imagini. Cum a fost la premiera din Paris|url=http://0-100.hotnews.ro/2012/09/27/video-foto-noile-sandero-si-logan-in-30-de-imagini-cum-a-fost-la-premiera-din-paris/|publisher=0–100.ro|date=27 September 2012}}</ref>

At the end of 2014, Dacia started to produce [[Euro 6]] engines, with reduced exhaust emissions.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.agerpres.ro/economie/2014/02/24/dacia-va-incepe-fabricarea-de-motoare-euro-6-la-finalul-anului-12-02-06|title=Dacia va începe fabricarea de motoare Euro 6 la finalul anului|website=www.agerpres.ro|access-date=24 March 2016|archive-date=8 April 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160408213239/http://www.agerpres.ro/economie/2014/02/24/dacia-va-incepe-fabricarea-de-motoare-euro-6-la-finalul-anului-12-02-06|url-status=dead}}</ref> From August 2015, the 0.9 TCe engine is equipped with the [[Start-stop system|Start & Stop]] system.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.promotor.ro/masini-noi/news/dacia-face-schimbari-in-gama-de-propulsoare-unitati-euro-6-si-doua-noi-motoare-cu-start-stop-14689751|title = Dacia face schimbări în gama de propulsoare: Unităţi Euro 6 şi două noi motoare cu Start-Stop|date = 26 August 2015}}</ref>

Starting from the end of 2016, the Dacia Logan range is offered with the ''[[Dacia Easy-R]]'' automated manual transmission (AMT).<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.daciagroup.com/presa/comunicate-de-presa/2016/noutatile-dacia-la-salonul-de-la-geneva-2016|title = Noutățile Dacia la Salonul de la Geneva 2016|date = 7 March 2016}}</ref><ref name="Easy-R">{{cite web|title=Dacia introduces new automatic manual Easy-R transmission|url=http://media.renault.com/global/en-gb/dacia/Media/PressRelease.aspx?mediaid=73734|publisher=media.renault.com|date=24 November 2015|access-date=29 September 2016|archive-date=6 February 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170206212631/http://media.renault.com/global/en-gb/dacia/Media/PressRelease.aspx?mediaid=73734|url-status=dead}}</ref>

===Variants===
In the European market, the new Logan is available in different trim levels: Access, Ambiance, Laureate, Stepway, Prestige. The Access level comes with black bumpers and power steering, and is available only with the 1.2-litre engine. Ambiance has body-coloured bumpers, wheel covers, Eco mode function, power [[vehicle door|lock door]]s, front [[vehicle door|power window]]s or [[CD player]], and as options there are [[metallic paint]], [[fog light]]s and air conditioning. Laureate adds body-coloured [[door handle]]s, [[fog light]]s as standard and trip computer, and additionally can be ordered with [[metallic paint]], Media Nav system, leather upholstery, parking sensors, cruise control or alloy wheels. This is the only equipment level available for the {{convert|90|hp|kW|0|abbr=on}} version of the 1.5-litre diesel engine.<ref name="versiuni">{{cite web|title=Noul Logan – Versiuni şi echipamente|url=http://www.dacia.ro/modele-si-preturi/noul-logan/versiuni-si-echipamente/acces/index.jsp|publisher=Dacia|access-date=14 November 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130720211507/http://www.dacia.ro/modele-si-preturi/noul-logan/versiuni-si-echipamente/acces/index.jsp|archive-date=20 July 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref>

In June 2014, a limited edition was made available in order to celebrate 10 years since the model's launch.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.wall-street.ro/articol/Auto/167742/dacia-a-lansat-seria-limitata-logan-10-ani-si-primul-model-cu-aer-conditionat-automat.html|title=Dacia a lansat seria limitata LOGAN 10 ANI si primul model cu aer cond|date=18 June 2014|work=Wall-Street|access-date=15 July 2015}}</ref> There will be produced only 2,000 units of this version, which features new equipment such as automatic air conditioning, double optic fog lights, mirror-mounted repeaters, 16-inch wheels, along with several special design elements like the different dashboard lighting (white instead of the then usual amber colour). This model was only available on the Romanian market and came equipped with 1.2 16v petrol and 1.5 dci diesel engines, both having 75 bhp. 

In October 2015, Dacia launched the new Prestige trim level, which has automatic air conditioning, mirror-mounted repeaters and 16-inch wheels.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Meșter |first1=Mircea |title=Dacia lansează Logan Prestige, noua echipare de top: climatizare automată, comenzi pe uși, jante de 16 inch și semnalizatoare pe oglinzi |url=https://www.automarket.ro/stiri/dacia-lanseaza-logan-prestige-noua-echipare-de-top-climatizare-automata-66843.html |website=Automarket |access-date=14 August 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200215135258/http://www.automarket.ro/stiri/dacia-lanseaza-logan-prestige-noua-echipare-de-top-climatizare-automata-66843.html |archive-date=15 February 2020 |language=Romanian |date=22 October 2015 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== <span class="anchor" id="Logan II MCV"></span><span class="anchor" id="second generation MCV"></span>Logan MCV ===
The estate version of the car made its debut at the [[Geneva Motor Show#2013|2013 Geneva Motor Show]]. The car will keep the MCV name, although it now stands for ''Maximum Capacity Vehicle'', rather than the previous ''Multi Convivial Vehicle''. It has 5 seats and a luggage capacity between {{convert|573|L|cuft}} and {{convert|1518|L|cuft}},<ref>{{cite web|date=5 March 2013|title=Dacia Logan MCV revealed|url=http://www.whatcar.com/car-news/dacia-logan-mcv-revealed/265418|publisher=What Car?}}</ref> featuring the same standard equipment and engine range as the [[sedan (car)|saloon]].<ref>{{cite web|date=5 March 2013|title=Dacia îşi continuă ofensiva cu Noul Logan MCV şi Duster Aventure|url=http://www.dacia.ro/despre-noi/noutati/2013/martie/dacia-continua-ofensiva-logan-mcv-duster-aventure/index.jsp|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130928025200/http://www.dacia.ro/despre-noi/noutati/2013/martie/dacia-continua-ofensiva-logan-mcv-duster-aventure/index.jsp|archive-date=28 September 2013|access-date=5 March 2013|publisher=Dacia}}</ref> It began to be marketed from the second half of 2013.<ref>{{cite web|date=5 March 2013|title=Dacia a lansat noul Logan MCV.|url=http://www.economica.net/dacia-lanseaza-astazi-doua-modele-urmareste-conferinta-live-aici_47074.html|publisher=Economica.net}}</ref>

