===Marketing and production===
Sales in Romania began in November 2012, with a starting price of €6,690.<ref>{{cite web|title=Dacia accelerează cu noile Logan, Sandero şi Sandero Stepway|url=http://www.daciagroup.com/presa/comunicate-de-presa/2012/dacia-accelereaza-cu-noile-logan-sandero-si-sandero-stepway|publisher=Dacia|date=8 November 2012}}</ref> It is manufactured in [[Mioveni]], Romania, and in [[Casablanca]], Morocco, at the [[Somaca]] factory, for the North African market.<ref name="paris"/> There will be no seven-seat or panel van versions of the second generation Logan, as they have been replaced by the [[Dacia Lodgy|Lodgy]] and the [[Dacia Dokker|Dokker]] respectively.<ref name="automobile"/>

The [[sedan (car)|saloon]] version was also launched in [[South America]], as the second generation Renault Logan, in December 2013,<ref name="renault_blog">{{cite web|title=New Logan : successful launches in South America|url=http://blog.renault.com/en/2014/01/14/new-logan-successful-launches-in-south-america/|publisher=Renault|access-date=31 January 2014|date=14 January 2014|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140201210603/http://blog.renault.com/en/2014/01/14/new-logan-successful-launches-in-south-america/|archive-date=1 February 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref> after being revealed at the Buenos Aires Motor Show in June 2013.<ref>{{cite web|title=Salão de Buenos Aires: novo Renault Logan chega ainda este ano|url=http://carplace.virgula.uol.com.br/salao-de-buenos-aires-novo-sandero-aparece-pela-primeira-vez-vestido-de-renault/|publisher=CARPLACE|access-date=31 January 2014|language=pt|date=19 June 2013|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130623231009/http://carplace.virgula.uol.com.br/salao-de-buenos-aires-novo-sandero-aparece-pela-primeira-vez-vestido-de-renault/|archive-date=23 June 2013|url-status=dead}}</ref> It is manufactured at the [[Renault do Brasil|Renault Brazil]] factory in [[São José dos Pinhais]] (near [[Curitiba]]).<ref name="renault_blog"/>

In March 2014, it was launched in [[Russia]] (where it is marketed as the Renault Logan). The model is produced at the [[AvtoVAZ]] facility in [[Togliatti (city)|Togliatti]], [[Samara Oblast|Samara]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://blog.alliance-renault-nissan.com/blog/renault-unveils-new-logan-russia|title=Renault unveils New Logan for Russia|work=Blog of RENAULT NISSAN|access-date=15 July 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140328000359/http://blog.alliance-renault-nissan.com/blog/renault-unveils-new-logan-russia|archive-date=28 March 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Also in 2014, the model was launched in [[Egypt]] (as the Renault Logan),<ref name="renault.com.eg">{{cite web|url=http://www.renault.com.eg/cars/logan/overview.html|title=Renault - OVERVIEW|access-date=15 July 2015}}</ref> together with the second generation of the [[Dacia Sandero|Sandero]] and Sandero Stepway.<ref name="renault.com.eg"/>

Production of the Logan started in [[Algeria]] in November 2014.<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 November 2014 |title=Inauguration of Oran plant marks start of automotive industry in Algeria |url=https://media.renaultgroup.com/inauguration-of-oran-plant-marks-start-of-automotive-industry-in-algeria/ |access-date=2026-02-25 |website=Newsroom Renault Group |language=en-GB}}</ref> Sold as the [[Renault Symbol]], the [[Knock-down kit|SKD]] assembly of the car at the {{Interlanguage link|Renault Algérie|fr|Usine Renault Algérie Production}} plant in [[Oran]] lasted until 2020, when the plant was closed due to new regulations surrounding the assembly of cars in Algeria.{{Citation needed|date=February 2026}} Although production temporarily restarted in 2021 before stopping shortly after,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Merabet |first=Aicha |date=2021-05-23 |title=L’usine Renault Algérie reprend son activité : ce qu’il faut savoir |url=https://www.tsa-algerie.com/lusine-renault-algerie-reprend-son-activite-ce-quil-faut-savoir/ |access-date=2026-02-25 |website=TSA |language=fr-FR}}</ref> {{As of|2025|lc=y}}, the plant remains closed due to ongoing disputes between Renault and the [[Algerian government]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Merabet |first=Aicha |date=2025-07-19 |title=Retour de Renault en Algérie : Tebboune intransigeant |url=https://www.tsa-algerie.com/retour-de-renault-en-algerie-tebboune-intransigeant/ |access-date=2026-02-25 |website=TSA |language=fr-FR}}</ref>

In August 2015, the new Logan was presented in [[Colombia]],<ref name="Revista Motor">{{cite web|title=Renault presentó en Colombia su nuevo y evolucionado Renault Logan|url=http://www.eltiempo.com/revista-motor/actualidad/lanzamientos/nuevo-renault-logan/23291|publisher=El Tiempo|access-date=23 August 2015|date=21 August 2015}}</ref> with the pre-sale of a thousand units. It is manufactured in Envigado at the [[SOFASA|Renault SOFASA]] factory.{{Citation needed|date=March 2016}}

In 2021, [[Coscharis Motors]] started [[Knock-down kit|SKD]] assembly in Awoyaya, [[Lagos]] (Nigeria).<ref>{{Cite news|title=Coscharis Motors to increase assembling variants in Nigeria|url=https://punchng.com/coscharis-motors-to-increase-assembling-variants-in-nigeria/|newspaper=[[The Punch]]|language=en-US|date=2022-06-20|access-date=2022-08-17}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Document d'enregistrement universel 2021|url=https://www.renaultgroup.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/renault_deu_2021.pdf|website=Renault Group|language=fr|date=March 2022|access-date=17 August 2022|archive-date=14 December 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221214125655/https://www.renaultgroup.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/renault_deu_2021.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref>

Production in [[Córdoba, Argentina|Cordoba]], Argentina stopped in December 2025.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Argentina - Córdoba Plant |url=https://www.renaultgroup.com/en/group/locations/cordoba-plant/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520203930/https://www.renaultgroup.com/en/group/locations/cordoba-plant/ |archive-date=2026-05-20 |access-date=2026-05-20 |work=Renault Group |language=en-US}}</ref>

====Turkey====
The third generation [[Renault Symbol]] is a rebadged version of the second generation Logan.<ref>{{cite web|title=2013 Renault Symbol revealed – rebadged Dacia Logan for Turkey|url=http://www.worldcarfans.com/112110150070/2013-renault-symbol-revealed---rebadged-dacia-logan-for|publisher=Worldcarfans|date=1 November 2012|access-date=7 November 2012|archive-date=12 February 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150212141636/http://www.worldcarfans.com/112110150070/2013-renault-symbol-revealed---rebadged-dacia-logan-for|url-status=dead}}</ref> It was revealed at the 2012 Istanbul Motor Show,<ref name="istanbul">{{cite web|title=New Renault Symbol: a status-enhancing yet affordable family saloon|url=http://media.renault.com/global/en-gb/Media/PressRelease.aspx?mediaid=39236|publisher=Renault|date=1 November 2012|access-date=7 November 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140201191402/http://media.renault.com/global/en-gb/Media/PressRelease.aspx?mediaid=39236|archive-date=1 February 2014|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Renault Symbol / Thalia|url=http://www.renault.com/en/vehicules/aujourd-hui/renault-vehicules-particuliers/pages/symbol-thalia.aspx|publisher=Renault|access-date=22 November 2012}}</ref> It went on sale on the Turkish market at the beginning of 2013, also being released in Tunisia, Algeria, the Middle East, and Chile, but not Morocco.<ref name="istanbul"/>

