The third-generation Logan was launched together with the new [[Dacia Sandero#Third generation (DJF; 2020)|Dacia Sandero III]], on 29 September 2020.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/dacia/sandero/109074/new-dacia-sandero-gets-sub-ps9k-price-tag|title=New Dacia Sandero gets sub £9k price tag|website=Auto Express}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=ALL-NEW SANDERO, SANDERO STEPWAY AND LOGAN : DACIA REDEFINES THE ESSENTIAL & C...|url=https://en.media.groupe.renault.com/news/all-new-sandero-sandero-stepway-and-logan-dacia-redefines-the-essential-contemporary-car-d216-989c5.html|access-date=2020-09-29|website=en.media.groupe.renault.com|language=en|archive-date=14 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210114131156/https://en.media.groupe.renault.com/news/all-new-sandero-sandero-stepway-and-logan-dacia-redefines-the-essential-contemporary-car-d216-989c5.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> It is longer by {{convert|36|mm|in|1|abbr=on}}, supported by a longer wheelbase and a reduced rear overhang. It has a slimmer shape, featuring a more sloping windscreen and a roof lowered by {{convert|10|mm|in|1|abbr=on}}.

It is built on a [[Renault–Nissan Common Module Family#CMF-B|CMF-B LS]] modular platform used by the new Sandero, and is claimed to combine greater strength and rigidity with less weight while complying with more stringent crash-test.  The new powertrain reduces emissions, and as of 2021 is compliant with pollution control requirements.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Dacia Logan (2021)|url=https://www.netcarshow.com/dacia/2021-logan/|access-date=2020-10-03|website=NetCarShow.com|language=en}}</ref>
===2022 refresh===
In June 2022, the Logan received a slight update incorporating the brand's new logo alongside other Dacia models. To accommodate the new logo, the grille is redesigned.<ref>{{cite web |date=15 June 2022 |title=Présentation - Le nouveau visage des Dacia |url=https://www.caradisiac.com/presentation-le-nouveau-visage-des-dacia-196623.htm |access-date=15 June 2022 |website=caradisiac.com |language=fr}}</ref>
