===Markets===

==== Dacia Logan ====
The third generation is available in fewer markets than its predecessor, at launch being offered only in Albania, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Kosovo, Moldova, Morocco, North Macedonia, Overseas French territories of the Pacific Ocean (French Polynesia and New Caledonia), Romania, Serbia and Tunisia.

In 2023, it was withdrawn from the Polish market due to "low customer interest".<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://francuskie.pl/czy-dacia-logan-na-powrot-pojawi-sie-w-polsce-mamy-odpowiedz-importera/|title=Czy Dacia Logan na powrót pojawi się w Polsce? Mamy odpowiedź importera! &#124; Francuskie.pl - Dziennik Motoryzacyjny|date=9 April 2024}}</ref> Also in 2023, the car was reintroduced to Israel after a five-year absence.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.ynetnews.com/business/article/s1xlgxdy3|title=Dacia revives family subcompact model, unveils tempting price|first=Noam|last=Rhein|newspaper=Ynetnews |date=8 July 2023|via=www.ynetnews.com}}</ref>

In 2024, at the request of dealers, a test batch of several hundred units was sent to Germany.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.profit.ro/povesti-cu-profit/auto-transporturi/surpriza-dacia-logan-se-intoarce-pe-cea-mai-mare-piata-auto-din-europa-21626070|title=SURPRIZĂ Dacia Logan se întoarce pe cea mai mare piață auto din Europa|website=Profit.ro |date=12 June 2024 }}</ref> In the same year, the model was brought back to Portugal.<ref>{{Cite web |title=MSN |url=https://www.msn.com/en-us/autos/other/dacia-logan-is-back-and-already-has-prices/ar-BB1pB0Km?item=flightsprg-tipsubsc-v1a?season89c26d1ce19649ab8c6b1ea6904de419Thu&apiversion=v2&noservercache=1&domshim=1&renderwebcomponents=1&wcseo=1&batchservertelemetry=1&noservertelemetry=1 |access-date=2025-10-16 |website=www.msn.com}}</ref>

==== Renault Taliant ====
Outside of Turkey, the Taliant is only offered in a very limited number of countries, located in Eastern Europe (such as Ukraine,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Новий TALIANT |url=https://www.renault.ua/passenger/taliant.html |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=www.renault.ua |language=uk-UA}}</ref> Georgia<ref>{{Cite web |date=7 April 2025 |title=Renault Taliant |url=https://renault.ge/cars/taliant-ljf-ph1/overview.html |access-date=7 April 2025 |website=Renault Georgia}}</ref>), Middle-East (Egypt,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Renault Taliant |url=https://www.renault.com.eg/cars/taliant-ljf-ph1/overview.html |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=www.renault.com.eg |language=en}}</ref> Jordan<ref>{{Cite web |title=Renault Taliant |url=https://renault.jo/cars/taliant-ljf-ph1/overview.html |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=renault.jo}}</ref>) and Africa (Nigeria,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Renault Taliant |url=https://www.renault.com.ng/cars/taliant-ljf-ph1/overview.html |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=www.renault.com.ng}}</ref> Gabon<ref>{{Cite web |title=Renault Taliant |url=https://www.renault.ga/cars/taliant-ljf-ph1/overview.html |access-date=2025-04-07 |website=www.renault.ga |language=fr}}</ref>).

====Russia====
The Logan, along with the [[Dacia Sandero|Sandero]], was supposed to launch in Russia in 2022, but this was never completed due to the [[2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine|ongoing war]] and the sale of [[Renault Russia]]. However, some camouflaged prototypes were photographed at the former Renault factory in Moscow, now [[Moskvitch]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://motor.ru/news/na-zavode-moskvich-sfotografirovali-novye-renault-logan-i-sandero-18-08-2022.htm|title=На заводе «Москвич» сфотографировали новые Renault Logan и Sandero|website=motor.ru}}</ref> A cross-sedan based on the Dacia Logan was also supposed to launch in [[Russia]], with camouflaged prototypes even photographed.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.auto-moto.com/nouveautes/scoop/renault-taliant-x-2023-cette-berline-captur-sera-t-vendue-france-363655.html|title=Renault Taliant X (2023) : une berline Captur bientôt en France ?|date=August 19, 2022}}</ref> A leaked image of the final car has been found in the [[Dacia Jogger]]'s owner's manual, as revealed by French forum Worldscoop.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://worldscoop.forumpro.fr/t13551-2022-renault-ljf-cross?highlight=renault|title=2022 Renault LJF Cross|website=worldscoop.forumpro.fr}}</ref> A subcompact sedan developed independently by [[AvtoVAZ]] on the same platform was presented in 2024 and badged as the [[Lada Iskra]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.carscoops.com/2024/06/lada-iskra-sedan-debuts-in-russia-based-on-renault-bones/ |title= Lada Iskra Sedan Debuts In Russia Based On Renault Bones |date=7 June 2024|website=Carscoops |access-date=2024-06-14 }}</ref>

